# ~ingest/.ssh/authorized_keys on the storage host.
#
# `restrict` turns off port forwarding, agent forwarding, X11, PTY allocation
# and user-rc; `command=` replaces whatever the client asked to run with the
# wrapper, which then allows exactly one thing: fk-archive by way of sudo.
# Reads do not come this way -- the archive is mounted from the NFS export --
# so there is no SFTP subsystem to allow. See fk_archive_utils/ssh_command.py.
#
# The account needs a real shell (/bin/sh is enough) for this to work: sshd
# runs a forced command through the login shell, so /usr/sbin/nologin would
# refuse it. The forced command is what keeps that shell from being reachable.

restrict,command="/usr/bin/fk-archive-ssh prod" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3Nz...  ingest@prod-kube-1
